No, but she's grizzly, but...

01:11:49.420 --> 01:11:57.850
Jules, you must know that perhaps you don't, but the truth is I hold you in the highest possible regard.

01:11:59.160 --> 01:12:00.000
I couldn't care less about your time.

01:12:01.370 --> 01:12:05.210
I find it funny, smart, and surprisingly funky, which is a rare combination.

01:12:10.780 --> 01:12:16.870
I believe they're playing our song.

01:12:17.640 --> 01:12:18.560
We have had a song.

01:12:18.820 --> 01:12:19.340
We do now.

01:13:22.910 --> 01:13:26.670
I suggest you keep a tighter rein on your son.

01:13:26.670 --> 01:13:28.040
What on earth are you talking?

01:13:53.840 --> 01:13:54.480
It's in there.

01:14:01.370 --> 01:14:04.800
Jules. Jules, wait.

01:14:06.540 --> 01:14:11.280
You should go back in. I'm sure they're looking for you.

01:14:12.750 --> 01:14:13.820
I'll just hang right here.

01:14:16.290 --> 01:14:22.560
Then hang with you, if that's all right.

01:14:35.720 --> 01:14:37.660
- But Arabella?

01:14:37.660 --> 01:14:39.000
- It's over.

01:14:39.000 --> 01:14:40.910
- What happened?

01:14:40.910 --> 01:14:41.810
- You've scundered with my heart.

01:14:41.810 --> 01:14:46.540
- How did I do that?

01:14:46.540 --> 01:14:51.640
You're the Prince of Calvary, I'm just a poor girl from Buffalo.

01:14:51.640 --> 01:14:52.880
- Exactly.

01:15:17.210 --> 01:15:18.950
- It's an outrage.

01:15:18.950 --> 01:15:21.710
Prince Ashton is flagrantly cavorting with that,

01:15:21.710 --> 01:15:23.110
with that trumpet.

01:15:23.110 --> 01:15:26.010
- Well, he's expected to be engaging our daughter.

01:15:26.010 --> 01:15:29.200
- My son has a mind reserve.

01:15:29.200 --> 01:15:29.830
- Oh, yes.

01:15:30.160 --> 01:15:34.420
We know all about your sons and their fascination with the great and washed.

01:15:34.740 --> 01:15:35.840
Bite your tongue, woman.

01:15:36.480 --> 01:15:41.480
I am the most honorable Duchess of Belmont, and it would behoove you to address me as such.

01:15:41.640 --> 01:15:48.170
You may well be a Duchess, but Jules Daly is more of a lady than you will ever be.

01:15:49.310 --> 01:15:52.260
You obviously don't know the real Jules Daly.

01:15:53.270 --> 01:15:54.530
She's clearly after your money.

01:15:54.830 --> 01:15:55.990
Why else do you think that girl is here?

01:15:56.480 --> 01:16:00.000
And anyone can see that she can't manage those children on her own.

01:16:00.800 --> 01:16:09.240
So, I did a little personal research, and did you know that Miss Jules Daly was fired from her job?

01:16:09.240 --> 01:16:18.500
Master Milo is in fact a kleptomaniac, or that little Maddie is a trans fat junkie.

01:16:18.500 --> 01:16:19.760
That is a lie.

01:16:19.760 --> 01:16:20.620
No.

01:16:20.620 --> 01:16:21.620
Oh dear.

01:16:21.620 --> 01:16:22.620
Carabella's right.

01:16:22.620 --> 01:16:23.620
See?

01:16:23.620 --> 01:16:25.210
Told you.

01:16:25.210 --> 01:16:29.350
Milo did steal that video game, but he returned it.

01:16:30.060 --> 01:16:34.240
and Maddie does have a temporary fascination with chips

01:16:34.240 --> 01:16:35.120
which we're trying to fix

01:16:35.120 --> 01:16:36.570
and I am currently unemployed

01:16:36.570 --> 01:16:37.910
but I hope for not too long

01:16:37.910 --> 01:16:39.110
because I really like working

01:16:39.110 --> 01:16:42.340
I may not know much about parenting

01:16:42.340 --> 01:16:45.010
but I know we don't need money to make us happy

01:16:45.010 --> 01:16:48.770
and we do need each other

01:16:48.770 --> 01:16:52.640
these are brave kids

01:16:52.640 --> 01:16:54.670
we deserve a chance at a family

01:16:54.670 --> 01:16:58.280
and as inconceivable as that may seem, Maribel

01:16:58.280 --> 01:16:59.960
that's the only reason we're here

01:17:00.250 --> 01:17:11.130
Ashton, you don't honestly believe her.

01:17:11.130 --> 01:17:13.880
Yes, I do.

01:17:13.880 --> 01:17:18.360
Edward? Surely you can see that she's-

01:17:18.360 --> 01:17:20.170
So who cares?

01:17:20.170 --> 01:17:22.770
You say Jules is a bad mother.

01:17:22.770 --> 01:17:28.280
Well, I've been a lousy father, and an even worse father-in-law.

01:17:28.280 --> 01:17:30.000
So Jules lost a job.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:32.940
You have never worked a single day in your life.

01:17:33.220 --> 01:17:36.760
And if you ask me, lady, Arabella Marchand of Belmont,

01:17:37.100 --> 01:17:40.820
you're the one who is all fur coat and no knickers.

01:17:49.900 --> 01:17:58.810
Thank you, Father.

01:18:00.640 --> 01:18:04.580
No. Thank you for putting up with an old fool.

01:18:04.580 --> 01:18:09.220
Now if I might give you a bit of fatherly advice,

01:18:09.220 --> 01:18:12.930
don't let that girl get away.

01:18:12.930 --> 01:18:23.430
May I speak to your own jewels for a second?

01:18:23.430 --> 01:18:25.410
Yeah. Sure.

01:18:31.400 --> 01:18:37.700
Jules, I know we don't have hot wings or hockey in Castlebury, but we do have crumpets and cricket.

01:18:40.320 --> 01:18:49.680
Is it possible you, Milo, and Maddy would consider extending your stay in Castlebury Hall?

01:18:53.600 --> 01:18:57.740
Beautiful gown Jules is wearing.

01:18:58.960 --> 01:18:59.610
Yes, sir.

01:19:00.090 --> 01:19:00.490
Lovely.

01:19:00.730 --> 01:19:01.550
Excellent taste.

01:19:01.830 --> 01:19:03.290
I wonder where she obtained it.

01:19:04.900 --> 01:19:10.740
I suppose if you wish to be reimbursed, you should produce a receipt for me by morning.

01:19:13.000 --> 01:19:14.930
Come on back to work.

01:19:16.740 --> 01:19:18.810
Thank you, sir.

01:19:19.550 --> 01:19:21.160
You're a good man, Paisley.

01:19:23.390 --> 01:19:25.370
Must be time.

01:19:27.860 --> 01:19:28.800
Thank you.

01:19:42.380 --> 01:19:45.170
There is a Santa Claus.

01:20:00.160 --> 01:20:01.700
Where do all these presents come from?

01:20:03.070 --> 01:20:04.410
Edward, you're amazing.

01:20:04.730 --> 01:20:06.690
No, my dear, you're the one that's amazing.

01:20:10.460 --> 01:20:12.520
What is it, Father?

01:20:13.050 --> 01:20:16.000
I just wish Charles...

01:20:16.000 --> 01:20:16.900
I wish he were here.

01:20:17.180 --> 01:20:17.860
What he is.

01:20:18.720 --> 01:20:21.220
Can you see him in the joy of Milo's eyes?

01:20:21.240 --> 01:20:21.460
Yeah.

01:20:23.110 --> 01:20:24.510
In the sparkle of Maddie's smile.

01:20:26.530 --> 01:20:27.310
Charles is here.

01:20:30.190 --> 01:20:39.470
so is my sister you're so right my dear ashton this is a very very wise girl we should not be

01:20:39.470 --> 01:20:49.210
lamenting what we have lost rather celebrating what we have found merry christmas christmas

01:21:57.100 --> 01:22:00.000
- It's like we're lying for a threat somewhere.

01:22:00.480 --> 01:22:02.580
As a matter of fact, they are.

01:22:03.250 --> 01:22:03.630
No.

01:22:04.970 --> 01:22:06.060
Really?

01:22:10.430 --> 01:22:23.070
It is true not all tales have happy endings.

01:22:23.870 --> 01:22:30.000
But then, for Jules Daly, the dreamer from Buffalo, the story is changed.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:31.700
Just beginning.

01:23:00.320 --> 01:23:01.120
Thank you.
